{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima","id":615016,"title":"Trinity Continuum: Anima","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Anima"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-04T07:13:39-07:00","id":615016,"title":"Trinity Continuum: Anima","content":"I teased one of our planned secondary settings at the Trinity Continuum/Scion/Scarred Lands panel at Gen Con. Understand that nothing's set in stone and things can still change.<br /> <br /> It's called <b>Anima</b>, and it's set in 2084 (the same year as <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Total_Recall_(1990_film)\" target=\"_blank\">Total Recall</a></i> and <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Remember_Me_(video_game)\" target=\"_blank\">Remember Me</a></i>). Other inspirations include the modern Abstergo bits of <i>Assassin's Creed</i>, and (to some degree) <i>The Matrix</i>.<br /> <br /> It's after the end of the Aberrant War, and humanity's still on the road to recovery, about 15 years before the first psions. People seek solace from the horrors of the war by using memory tech, but nothing is as straightforward as it seems on the surface.<br /> <br /> There's a reason people in <b>Aeon</b> are leery of invasive hardtech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":4,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","user":"IanWatson","date":". 08-04-2015, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T09:33:53-07:00","id":615218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima#post615016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I teased one of our planned secondary settings at the Trinity Continuum/Scion/Scarred Lands panel at Gen Con. Understand that nothing's set in stone and things can still change.<br /> <br /> It's called <b>Anima</b>, and it's set in 2084 (the same year as <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Total_Recall_(1990_film)\" target=\"_blank\">Total Recall</a></i> and <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Remember_Me_(video_game)\" target=\"_blank\">Remember Me</a></i>). Other inspirations include the modern Abstergo bits of <i>Assassin's Creed</i>, and (to some degree) <i>The Matrix</i>.<br /> <br /> It's after the end of the Aberrant War, and humanity's still on the road to recovery, about 15 years before the first psions. People seek solace from the horrors of the war by using memory tech, but nothing is as straightforward as it seems on the surface.<br /> <br /> There's a reason people in <b>Aeon</b> are leery of invasive hardtech.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, a Trinity game drawing on sources such as Philip K Dick novels? I'm in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T14:36:28-07:00","id":615566,"title":"","content":"Kinda meh. I like the idea and you can do a lot of things with it, but you putting it in core timeline is imo mistake. You absolutely NEED to showcase alternate timelines, otherwise we get stuck into the same fail, that was original timeline and its fail metaplot, which severely damages the whole idea of Continuum, before you even flesh it out.<br /> <br /> Also plothole Alert. All psitech is extremely invasive and this division feels very arbitrary and nonsensical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T15:26:19-07:00","id":615630,"title":"","content":"I'm fine with it; I have no problem with inserting eras between the existing ones, or adding new ones before Adventure!/after \u00c6on \u2014 though I agree with zorb42's contention that the first new era you publish probably <i>shouldn't</i> be in line with the core three, just to definitively establish the expanse of the Continuum. Much like how White Wolf followed Mage: the Awakening with Promethean: the Created, in part to establish that they were not going to be chained to the oWoD's publishing sequence. <br /> <br /> As for Anima, the line about invasive hardtech makes me think that it might be TC's take on cyberpunk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T20:34:17-07:00","id":615953,"title":"","content":"It's most likely post Aberrant War because they felt that was the best set-up for what they wanted to do with the setting. Getting hung up over whether to publish within a certain timeline or start branching out to alt timelines immediately is just creatively limiting for no good reason.<br /> <br /> I also don't care, frankly, because it's really easy to not have the Aberrant War really matter in my Aberrant game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T20:34:52-07:00","id":615954,"title":"","content":"Anima sounds really cool. I'm looking forward to seeing what they do with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T20:52:41-07:00","id":615962,"title":"","content":"Long time/first time and this is completely the wrong thread but...<br /> I never really got into Adventure! Of the 3 series, I found it the silliest, most difficult to reconcile with the continuity (though we called it something else then) and wasn't sure what to do with Paramorphs. And because of that, while I'm definitely going to buy Aeon, I was least jazzed about the default modern Talents setting. Until I saw Mission: Impossible Rogue Nations.<br /> <br /> Alec Baldwin's CIA Director Hunley refers to Ethan Hunt as <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&quot;the living manifestation of destiny,&quot;</div></div> </div> </div> and for some reason that has me absolutely tickled to give Daredevils a try in a modern setting. I realize that the original was modular enough that I could have just made it a modern setting but I'm a total stickler for canon and backstory. I don't think it'd take me more than 4 hours to create the Uber setting using Aberrant but keep saying &quot;heh, let's just say Slider wasn't murder after all and see where that takes us...&quot;<br /> <br /> At any rate, I'm very patiently very much looking forward to being able to play a Jason Statham-esque character within this system. Maybe he'll live long enough to bag a Nova.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T04:08:30-07:00","id":616226,"title":"","content":"Welcome to the board Queen Anne Country. Daredevil/Paramorph/Talents are a delightful breed and the quote captures them well. I'm sorry your post may get lost in the following 'serious business' on the internet...<br /> -smile-<br /> Post Aberrant war, Great leap upward time period is one i have spent much time with. This was the last sanctuary of hard science, utilized to take us into space. If you turn those possibilities into something resembling the Matrix or Total Recall, then i fear for hard science fiction in the greater continuum.<br /> Will the technology and elements from this period also be available in Aeon's 2120's? How many of the established series events in the later setting will be affected by the technology planned for this one? How are we going to refer to individual Aberrant Quantum power-suites when the same word now refers to another setting, will it be context sensitive?<br /> If you had listed others sources/influences on the setting, maybe it would allay my fears, but these were the post-crash years - the earth is tainted and scarred, the only hope worth pursuing may lie off-world. Why would we send out generational arks as a species if we are made to be comfortable here in the ashes of the world? I feel this could miss out on the potential of the crash and the desperate space-flight i had envisioned - and all i can do is hope it doesn't invalidate years of writing and thinking on my part.<br /> Matrix has some grungy sets, but few outside of it's machine world scenes seem like the world needs rebuilding and i can entirely do without it's psuedo intellectual ramblings and shallow characters (apologies to fans, personal opinion here). Clarifying whether you intended Total Recall as the Phillip K Dick book or the Schwarzenegger movie would be helpful - i would have assumed the former, but pairing it with the Matrix makes me uncertain as to your intent.<br /> Apologies for the cynicism, it's just one of those days. I look forward (in both excitement and fear) to hearing more about the details here - because this is the make or break extra era for me and i have no control over where it's headed.<br /> Screw the Sardonyx rules, i want open <i>setting</i> development.<br /> -blush-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Replied more to Queen Anne Country 08-05-2015, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T05:33:19-07:00","id":616348,"title":"","content":"That's a lot of supposition based on a couple of short sentences.<br /> <br /> I see no reason why anything we say has to invalidate anything you've decided upon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T08:15:39-07:00","id":616513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=616348#post616348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a lot of supposition based on a couple of short sentences.<br /> <br /> I see no reason why anything we say has to invalidate anything you've decided upon.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I feel this just made my case for me. Yes it does. This setting will establish, what did actually happen after Abberant war for Aeon backstory. It will be set in stone and unchangeable. Potential to actually fail this in eyes of many is hard and by putting it in core timeline YOU will set it in stone as core and hard backstory for Aeon. This is rather important and I am with nihilist on this, these influences really do not invoke setting, which would lead to Aeon well. You are deeply underestimating what people will think , if you do not keep information stream going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T09:30:12-07:00","id":616578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=616348#post616348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a lot of supposition based on a couple of short sentences.<br /> <br /> I see no reason why anything we say has to invalidate anything you've decided upon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like i said, it's been one of those days, please forgive my passion for Trinity. I don't know what was discussed on the panel, so i'm likely guilty of some knee-jerk reaction. I should've waited for more details before replying. Actually, what the publishers say does matter to me, because i'm expecting it to be pretty good so far. But, some more details would be helpful in nailing down exactly what we're discussing.<br /> I have no idea what to think based on the OP, Matrix and Total Recall and Remember Me are all over the place outside of their shared techno-psychological themes. I want to hear more, if not about the setting details themselves, then about intent and connectivity with the setting that we do actually know. I <i>am</i> a little sensitive on the period you chose, having thought a lot about it during 2120's preludes and re-reads, which is about all i know about those years.<br /> Without imagination on my part driving these suppositions there isn't much to reply to, with all due respect. I'm willing to consider a 2084 setting, it's one of my favourite periods, in which i saw some kind of technological hard sci-fi post apocalypse with in-system space travel - i like the notion of detailing the techno-phobia of the 2120s - because i embraced that, so much that i'm also iffy on how you will reintroduce ubiquitous wireless.<br /> -glares suspiciously at developers-<br /> But, i'm willing to listen, when you're ready to explain.<br /> I know you have reasons to keep mum, but some clarifications or expansion would certainly be interesting food for thought. The alternate settings are fascinating, but we know too little to discuss them with any consequence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  word substitution 08-05-2015, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T09:48:02-07:00","id":616611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=616513#post616513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It will be set in stone and unchangeable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last August, Ian said:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?734129-GenCon-Trinity-Continuum-Tease&amp;p=18219426#post18219426\" target=\"_blank\">I'm on board with having a few conflicting histories, which only serve to reinforce the quantum-wibbly nature of the Continuum.</a><br /> <br /> I had hoped that statement would prevent the cries of &quot;this invalidates my head canon&quot; that occur whenever a publisher updates a setting.<br /> <br /> Ian: sounds awesome. Looking forward to it.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T10:47:12-07:00","id":616665,"title":"","content":"There is no such thing as &quot;set in stone and unchangeable&quot; in any RPG, and that goes doubly for the Continuum.<br /> <br /> The timestream is a fluid thing. An infinite number of histories can lead to this present, which can spawn an infinite number of futures.<br /> <br /> We're showing you what we think is a fun setting which takes place in between Aberrant and Aeon. If it doesn't match what you'd already decided on, neat! Maybe yours is better. We're never going to say it's wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T11:10:34-07:00","id":616682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=616665#post616665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no such thing as &quot;set in stone and unchangeable&quot; in any RPG, and that goes doubly for the Continuum.<br /> <br /> The timestream is a fluid thing. An infinite number of histories can lead to this present, which can spawn an infinite number of futures.<br /> <br /> We're showing you what we think is a fun setting which takes place in between Aberrant and Aeon. If it doesn't match what you'd already decided on, neat! Maybe yours is better. We're never going to say it's wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has been a fun thread this evening, i hope i'm not dragging it down, i just want the setting to be as good as it can be.<br /> I don't really see what you have in mind for this setting that couldn't be done with late aberrant (comic book super-science heaven with kaiju) or pre-trinity (sci-fi recovery and early space colonization). I'm interested to see the results, because there are intelligent and creative ideas behind it. I just assumed you would be detailing settings that couldn't really work within the 'three pillar' settings (like the 70's-80's movie setting i've heard is in the core book), but Trinity already does hard sci-fi and post-apocalypse pretty well so my suggestions aren't any better, i admit. Perhaps i'd assumed an aberrant war setting was the most natural inbetween-time for Aberrant and Aeon.<br /> Bates used the term &quot;tonal distinctions&quot; in reference to the differences between Aberrant and Trinity, but the little i know leaves me wondering what else is different in Anima that it couldn't have just been a throwback Sci-Fi Aeon game.<br /> Thanks for the replies, Ian - it's always compelling to know you're listening.<br /> P.S. You seem to have a pretty good grip on the structure of time relating to the continuum, can't wait to hear more about that either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Okay, my edits are out of control... I think i need a break. -smile- 08-05-2015, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T11:36:33-07:00","id":616720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=616513#post616513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It will be set in stone and unchangeable. Potential to actually fail this in eyes of many is hard and by putting it in core timeline YOU will set it in stone as core and hard backstory for Aeon.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could always do what I do with anything from earlier timelines that doesn't mesh with your take on Aeon - ignore it. I ignored HUGE amounts of what came out in Aberrant (and later Trinity books) that didn't do it for me. For the players in our group that loved Aberrant, I just made sure they imagined it had never been published (and anything else mentioning Novas) when I ran Trinity games. Worked perfectly. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T11:52:13-07:00","id":616731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=616720#post616720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could always do what I do with anything from earlier timelines that doesn't mesh with your take on Aeon - ignore it. I ignored HUGE amounts of what came out in Aberrant (and later Trinity books) that didn't do it for me. For the players in our group that loved Aberrant, I just made sure they imagined it had never been published (and anything else mentioning Novas) when I ran Trinity games. Worked perfectly. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this has been solution to crappy writing since time Immemorial. It is also incredibly bad precedent for actual writers of the books to do. It not only leads imo to shoddy writing, but i feel in case of Trinity it does damage the core appeal of the system, which is the Core timeline+alt timelines, interconnectivity and multiple hard connected settings, which have full crossover potential and were written with that in mind, because they do work out of the same system and without that it does not have that much going for it, especially, because Aberant was the setting chosen as the odd man out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T12:03:16-07:00","id":616732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=616731#post616731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, this has been solution to crappy writing since time Immemorial.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woah there fella. I couldn't disagree more in this case. You don't like something, you leave it out. That's kinda the whole thing our hobby has going for it. If something doesn't match your vision is doesn't mean its poor writing, it just means you have a different take on it - good - thats kinda the point. I have very little time to spend creating setting, stories and so on myself, but even I can take the time to simply ignore something (read: novas). It really works, give it a try. My default to anyone asking 'so hey, how about playing one of those nova thingies in 2120 then?' was 'yeah they all blew up, sorry. So, about those Psi Orders you can pick from....'<br /> <br /> And my take is going to be very different from the writers and other GMs and that's OK (some of them even have a bizarre, unfathomable attachment to them nova thingies <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":232,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","user":"CHILL","date":".  typos, typos... duh. 08-05-2015, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T12:06:36-07:00","id":616734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=616732#post616732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And my take is going to be very different from the game writers, and other GMs and that's OK (some of them even have a bizarre, unfathomable attachment to them nova thingies <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It can work! I tell you, it can work!<br /> -returns to mad scientist's lab-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T12:07:07-07:00","id":616735,"title":"","content":"I think we will have to agree to disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T12:33:16-07:00","id":616747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=616735#post616735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we will have to agree to disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> <br /> Perhaps wait to take a look at what Anima actually is when there's a bit more out for it other than just Ian's quick announcement. You never know, you may like what you see <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T12:50:27-07:00","id":616754,"title":"","content":"If we were writing a series of novels, I agree, I'd probably take a stricter stance on how the timeline behaves. But I'm not; I'm making a game (or a series of games). RPGs are literally tools to enable you to tell your own stories with a group of friends. While I certainly hope people like the setting(s) we provide, I'm just as engaged in providing enough raw material that people can hack up and stitch back together to play however they want. I'm adamant that the Trinity Continuum is the coolest damn thing even if you don't like the exact thing we're giving to you. So yeah, I'm going to play up the &quot;quantum-wibbly&quot; nature of the Continuum as much as I can.<br /> <br /> Craig Oxbrow used to use Adventure! rules to run Star Wars games. That's awesome! CHILL wants to run Aeon without any novas. I'd like to see how that works! If you don't like Anima-as-written, well, I'm sorry because I personally think it's awesome, but I sincerely hope there's at least something in there you find cool enough to add to your own games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T13:19:48-07:00","id":616763,"title":"","content":"I can't think of a single setting or adventure that I've successfully run &quot;as is&quot; -- there's always something that should be ignored or added for my table's maximum enjoyment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T15:03:16-07:00","id":616825,"title":"","content":"Thinking of it now, actually...you don't suppose their will be any conflict with the game Anima: Beyond Fantasy? It's a series of table-top game related things: a card game, tactical miniatures game, and importantly a pen and paper RPG. It's from Spain, and imported to the US market by Fantasy Flight. I really hope you guys have heard of Fantasy Flight at least, because it would be sad otherwise.<br /> <br /> While I know that there shouldn't be anything legally wrong with the two works sharing a similar title (although poor Aeon got put over with far less), I do wonder if there may be other confusion or conflicts. If it might be a problem I'd rather see it addressed now before we get to used to the name Anima or risk breaking the A-theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T17:51:17-07:00","id":616972,"title":"","content":"Our booth at Gen Con is typically right next to the miniature city that is FFG, so yes, it would be quite hard to be unaware of them.<br /> <br /> As mentioned in my first post in this thread, this is all tentative. There's no guarantee that this setting will actually get made (although there is a good chance). If it does get made, we won't necessarily call it Anima. That's just the current working name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T19:21:19-07:00","id":617029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=616972#post616972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our booth at Gen Con is typically right next to the miniature city that is FFG, so yes, it would be quite hard to be unaware of them.<br /> <br /> As mentioned in my first post in this thread, this is all tentative. There's no guarantee that this setting will actually get made (although there is a good chance). If it does get made, we won't necessarily call it Anima. That's just the current working name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just wanted to bring it to your attention. You guys can hardly be expected to be aware of every RPG on the market these days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T22:08:15-07:00","id":618491,"title":"","content":"I like the concept and am sure that even if I don't use the setting as an era I will find something worth adding to my games. My games rarely feature anything from the main setting having established my own timeline starting approximately ten years after the original timeline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T08:42:40-07:00","id":623350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima#post615016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I teased one of our planned secondary settings at the Trinity Continuum/Scion/Scarred Lands panel at Gen Con. Understand that nothing's set in stone and things can still change.<br /> <br /> It's called <b>Anima</b>, and it's set in 2084 (the same year as <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Total_Recall_(1990_film)\" target=\"_blank\">Total Recall</a></i> and <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Remember_Me_(video_game)\" target=\"_blank\">Remember Me</a></i>). Other inspirations include the modern Abstergo bits of <i>Assassin's Creed</i>, and (to some degree) <i>The Matrix</i>.<br /> <br /> It's after the end of the Aberrant War, and humanity's still on the road to recovery, about 15 years before the first psions. People seek solace from the horrors of the war by using memory tech, but nothing is as straightforward as it seems on the surface.<br /> <br /> There's a reason people in <b>Aeon</b> are leery of invasive hardtech.</div> </div> </div> </div>A semi-cyber punk Aeon game could be fun. Some questions:<br /> <br /> Would the default PC in this case be human? All the old gamelines defaulted to something other than vanilla human.<br /> <br /> To what degree will Novas/Aberrants and the Aberrant war influence the setting? Is this an opportunity to see the destruction and horror the Nova Age brings, or an opportunity to actually be the mutated freaks, perhaps?<br /> <br /> Since this setting is chronologically book-ended, do you see this as a game where people could carry their characters into the age of the psions? Are you going to have some kind or hard setting shift in there (like the how the Aberrant ends the Nova Age)?<br /> <br /> What is the theme and mood of this game?<br /> <br /> What play experience/angle does it offer that will differentiate it from being, say a Cyberkinetic Nova, or a just plain techie in the world of Trinity?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T19:36:06-07:00","id":631831,"title":"","content":"The inspirations for the game sound a lot less like Cyberpunk 2020/Shadowrun hackers and corporate espionage kind of game, and more of a thing where enhanced technology can mess with your sense of reality, which is a much more common theme in Phillip K. Dick, as well as the Matrix franchise. Less, &quot;I downloaded the data, let's rock n' roll&quot; and more &quot;Is my ten year old daughter - and by extension my feelings for her and memories about her- real, or is she just an extremely elaborate Pepsi ad designed to manipulate my underlying unserved paternal needs?&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T21:57:57-07:00","id":631907,"title":"","content":"I get that, but we can do 'Black Mirror' style techno-thrillers with the 2120s setting. What sets Anima apart? Besides the promise of technological toys that would fit seamlessly into less technologically restrictive Aeon games, and no psions, why would i play Anima instead of Aeon?<br /> Don't get me wrong, perhaps this is closer to the hard sci-fi that i want out of a sci-fi rpg, but it seems that these settings could diminish one another in some ways. There were suggestions that some willingly submit themselves to 'Matrix' like hibernation, leaving their bodies behind with some often seedy individuals in Hidden Agendas (i think). It feels like we are pruning back Aeon and planting the clippings as Anima, but that's probably just because nothing so far has persuaded me otherwise. I consider 2084 to be part of the Aeon era, this is humanity rebuilding after an 'inspired' catastrophe, it was the era that catalyzed 'Hope, Unity, Sacrifice' as human values - it's sequentially needed.<br /> I'm not mad, but i am pretty confused as to what Anima is supposed to be to the rest of the TC, Aeon in particular. There are a few pretty well regarded Cyberpunk games available already (plus the America Offline material for Aeon 2120). What can i expect Anima to sell itself on, time-travel, the inspired? Well, at least it will be fascinating to see the mental gymnastics performed to fit cosmic elements like those into a Gibson-esque presentation. That would be LoEG level setting work.<br /> -smile-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T08:42:41-07:00","id":632335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=631907#post631907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that, but we can do 'Black Mirror' style techno-thrillers with the 2120s setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't have enough information about 2120 in the TC to make that statement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=631907#post631907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What sets Anima apart? Besides the promise of technological toys that would fit seamlessly into less technologically restrictive Aeon games, and no psions, why would i play Anima instead of Aeon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like you answered your own question. &quot;More tech + no psionics&quot; may not be attractive enough for you, but it sounds like a good solid alt campaign to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T09:40:46-07:00","id":632400,"title":"","content":"The way you put it, it seems you expect the TC to be at odds with the setting that brought most of us to the table. While i'm open minded about a few healthy revisions/changes, what on earth could i actually discuss here if not for the information i already have access to. Is 2120 really going to change so much that previously accessible concepts may no longer be accessible? I certainly hope not, versatility is perhaps the greatest strength of the original 'three pillar' settings.<br /> I'm not saying it doesn't appeal, on the contrary, i've personally run a few 2120s tech based games with Psionics playing only a background role and the material supports that, if Anima is decent i may find myself entirely converted to this period/timeline (take that, Doyen). But to ensconce &quot;more tech + less psionics&quot; as a primary seperation of an alternate setting just seems to dilute the Sci-Fi potential of Aeon (as opposed to the comic potential of Aberrant and pulp potential of Adventure). I want the tech, but what is so momentous that it couldn't just be a supplement for Aeon? There are neutrals in 2120 and a group of all neutrals should still be an interesting scenario in any era, not just an alternate setting. The tech is just restricted, superscience in Aeon should be free to shatter those legal restrictions and face the consequences - so why seperate the two?<br /> Prior to OPP, the main unifying factor (apart from inspiration) for the series was its timeline, i understand that this is going to be more or less obsolete in the time-travel-ready TC. But until i see more 'structure of time' details should i just ignore sequential history as detailed in the original books?<br /> Again, don't get me wrong, i like the notion and i'm interested to hear more - but the distinctions aren't as clear as i'd like. I just don't want to see the setting diminish the possibilities of Aeon, by sequestering it's own slice of the sci-fi pie. I want to see Aeon reach it's potential, i like Anima, but not if it comes at the expense of era versatility.<br /> -shrug-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T13:40:55-07:00","id":632697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=632400#post632400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way you put it, it seems you expect the TC to be at odds with the setting that brought most of us to the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>At odds? No, but the fact that Anima is being proposed indicates that its style of game may be . . . well, not &quot;unsupported&quot; but perhaps not a focus in the main Aeon setting. Or maybe it won't be supported at all.<br /> <br /> Bottom line: we don't have enough information to know. And over-analysing the little information we do have can lead to elaborate head-canon that interferes with the actual final product's reception.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=632400#post632400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While i'm open minded about a few healthy revisions/changes, what on earth could i actually discuss here if not for the information i already have access to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am taking the position of discussing what has been revealed, and not much more. If OP wants more discussion on TC, they can reveal more details <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> You are, of course, free to speculate based on the previous edition as you'd like and ignore my conservative stance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=632400#post632400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't want to see the setting diminish the possibilities of Aeon, by sequestering it's own slice of the sci-fi pie. I want to see Aeon reach it's potential, i like Anima, but not if it comes at the expense of era versatility.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope Aeon -- all the settings, actually -- will be more focused and less kitchen sink. If OP pull kaiju/mech battles and cyberdecking out of Aeon, I will rejoice. I'd be a bit sadder to see &quot;Interplanetary Colonists&quot; get pushed to the &quot;Aeon + 100years&quot; setting, but as long as we've got psions fighting Earth's foes, both without and within, I'll be happy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T14:16:53-07:00","id":632715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaulChapman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=632697#post632697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be a bit sadder to see &quot;Interplanetary Colonists&quot; get pushed to the &quot;Aeon + 100years&quot; setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're not currently planning an &quot;Aeon + 100 years&quot; setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T23:00:54-07:00","id":633149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaulChapman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=632697#post632697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> <br /> Bottom line: we don't have enough information to know. And over-analysing the little information we do have can lead to elaborate head-canon that interferes with the actual final product's reception.<br /> <br /> I am taking the position of discussing what has been revealed, and not much more. If OP wants more discussion on TC, they can reveal more details <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> You are, of course, free to speculate based on the previous edition as you'd like and ignore my conservative stance.<br /> <br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct, as passionate as i am about the era, there just isn't really a lot here yet. Ian has already said this is a long term target, so i'm not getting worked up, just inferring for the sake of discussion. I have no idea whether anything i have said is pertinent or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I hope Aeon -- all the settings, actually -- will be more focused and less kitchen sink. </div> </div> </div>On that, we may have to disagree, but this is a fascinating proposition. Do you think i could encourage you to dare stepping out of your conservatory safety to speculate how that might be done?<br /> -smile-<br /> Thanks for the reply, Mr. Chapman.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=632715#post632715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We're not currently planning an &quot;Aeon + 100 years&quot; setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, &quot;reasons&quot; prevent too much discussion, but are you just being overly precise here? I thought there were plans for a setting <i>after</i> Aeon, like a far-future star-wars space opera thing or something in the space fantasy genre or whatever else your twisted imaginations have come up with for the distant future. Clearly not exactly &quot;Aeon + 100 years&quot;, but something beyond the 2100s.<br /> -shrug-<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Aeon + 100 years 08-20-2015, 02:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T23:44:59-07:00","id":633201,"title":"","content":"There's rough plans for a post-Aeon setting, yes, but &quot;far future&quot; means <i>far</i> future. You'd be more likely to see something that's closer 4240 than 2120. &quot;Aeon +100 years&quot; or +200 years or whatever is not something we're looking at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T00:59:34-07:00","id":633257,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the clarification, post-Aeon &amp; far future didn't come with any qualifying numbers. I had pictured a kind of Aasimov 'foundation' era - so far ahead that humanities origins are shrouded in mystery (except probably for whatever Aeon becomes). But that's just my imagination filling in the details again...<br /> -smile-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T06:31:41-07:00","id":633382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=633201#post633201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's rough plans for a post-Aeon setting, yes, but &quot;far future&quot; means <i>far</i> future. You'd be more likely to see something that's closer 4240 than 2120. &quot;Aeon +100 years&quot; or +200 years or whatever is not something we're looking at.</div> </div> </div> </div>Advancing the timeline more than a couple hundred years, and keeping it linked to Aeon in a significant way, snaps my suspenders of disbelief. Culture can change quite a bit in 100 years, especially with modern+ levels of technology. Increase that by a factor of 10, and my group will have as much in common with those characters as we do with mammals fighting dinosaurs.<br /> <br /> But that's just me. I avoid Traveller (but not Babylon 5) and Bunnies and Burrows for the same reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T10:13:59-07:00","id":633567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaulChapman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=633382#post633382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Advancing the timeline more than a couple hundred years, and keeping it linked to Aeon in a significant way, snaps my suspenders of disbelief. Culture can change quite a bit in 100 years, especially with modern+ levels of technology. Increase that by a factor of 10, and my group will have as much in common with those characters as we do with mammals fighting dinosaurs.<br /> <br /> But that's just me. I avoid Traveller (but not Babylon 5) and Bunnies and Burrows for the same reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We don't expect everyone to get on board with every era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T09:00:05-07:00","id":634641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaulChapman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=633382#post633382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's just me. I avoid Traveller (but not Babylon 5) and Bunnies and Burrows for the same reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aww, come on. There's always room for some Bun-Fu <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T08:58:32-07:00","id":637069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=632400#post632400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying it doesn't appeal, on the contrary, i've personally run a few 2120s tech based games with Psionics playing only a background role and the material supports that, if Anima is decent i may find myself entirely converted to this period/timeline (take that, Doyen). But to ensconce &quot;more tech + less psionics&quot; as a primary seperation of an alternate setting just seems to dilute the Sci-Fi potential of Aeon (as opposed to the comic potential of Aberrant and pulp potential of Adventure).<br /> -</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, I'm not reading the take-away as &quot;More tech, less psionics&quot;. I'm thinking it really is going to do some things that Aeon does not currently do. You guys are getting way too hung up on Gibsonian cyberpunk that you aren't really seeing the possibilities.<br /> <br /> Given the name &quot;Anima&quot; refers directly to the Jungian model of the unconscious/subconscious mind, and the refernces to other works around the theme of memory - Total Recall, Remember Me, and Assassin's Creed's &quot;genetic memory&quot; bits*...it's my thought that exploration of memory and personality will be the bigger player than mega-corps and mirrorshades.<br /> <br /> What about Aeon agents needing to extract valuable individuals from therapeutic simulators?<br /> What about Aberrant agents seeding augmented reality to produce sleeper agents?<br /> What about powers based on genetic memory?<br /> <br /> I drool in anticipation.<br /> <br /> *Abstergo in Assassin's Creed also uses the &quot;Animus System&quot;, which is another reference to Jung.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","user":"Wolfgar","date":". 08-23-2015, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T06:55:14-07:00","id":670923,"title":"","content":"Late to respond, but Wolfgar's picking up on a <i>lot</i> of what I'm putting down.<br /> <br /> Cyberpunkish conspiracy stories can still be done with Aberrant and Aeon, sure. But that's not the intended focus of <b>Anima</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Anima</b>'s also going to hint at the possible origins of-- but I say too much.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T00:31:55-07:00","id":671702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=637069#post637069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...it's my thought that exploration of memory and personality will be the bigger player than mega-corps and mirrorshades.</div> </div> </div> </div>I caught that and i apologize if i'm generalizing to make it sound that way. The cyberpunk genre aligns with some of the concepts herein, but i'm aware that's just short-hand. I am very curious to see how the era is used, despite the issues i've already brought up (etymology, tone, etc..).<br /> Thanks for the post Wolfgar, i can dig some psychological Sci-Fi (black mirror anyone?), i was already running some in Trinity. Hence; my arguement that Anima seems kind of derivative from the very little we know - because i can't see anything about it (yet) that would require another era to explore. I am happy to be proven wrong, but when all feedback seems positive, my devil's advocate awakens...<br /> -sly-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=670923#post670923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Late to respond, but Wolfgar's picking up on a <i>lot</i> of what I'm putting down.<br /> <br /> Cyberpunkish conspiracy stories can still be done with Aberrant and Aeon, sure. But that's not the intended focus of <b>Anima</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Anima</b>'s also going to hint at the possible origins of-- but I say too much.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I really want to like this post, but i'm not doing so under protest of non-committal, nebulous language. There just isn't enough here (concerning Anima) to say anything meaningful about (except in abstract), but it hasn't stopped me - repeatedly.<br /> I'll bet 1 (one) internet that you're alluding to memory/time technology. But, i'm still no closer to grasping the era of Anima - apart from insights from Wolfgar.<br /> Apologies if my mental obstacle here is detracting from the excitement of anyone, because i too am really looking forward to more information about Anima and it could potentially hook me deep. In my defense; i'm invested, which makes me care, which makes me post. I'd be talking more about it, but that would all be extrapolation from a scant few mentions - chief amongst them; reference to the Matrix and Total Recall. That was really where i got concerned, but that's because i personally feel both those movies (and remember me) took great ideas and failed to capitalize for one reason or another.<br /> -shrug-<br /> Despite my issues with Total Recall and Matrix, i think the recent Assassins Creed <i>is</i> closer to the right vein in my own perspective. But, i haven't played past AC4 yet...<br /> <br /> Nuanced &amp; thoughtful Sci-Fi, in the vein of Trinity but without Psionics?<br /> I'll take two.<br /> As long as you developer-bastards deliver.<br /> -smile-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  actually, 'Assassins Creed' works 09-20-2015, 03:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T16:38:53-07:00","id":675793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=670923#post670923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Anima</b>'s also going to hint at the possible origins of-- but I say too much.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly plenty to speculate here, although it might be groundless. The proxies, perhaps? I believe their origins were somewhat obfuscated in the original game, and this is roughly the time period for them to be getting started according to the blurb. Of course that is one option among a few.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T10:18:17-07:00","id":676540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=675793#post675793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Certainly plenty to speculate here, although it might be groundless. The proxies, perhaps? I believe their origins were somewhat obfuscated in the original game, and this is roughly the time period for them to be getting started according to the blurb. Of course that is one option among a few.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weren't proxies histories documented rather well in their order and locale books? The only hidden things were the actual transformation, but I do not think that is good theme for differrent game to work with and wasn't that later anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T15:17:12-07:00","id":676889,"title":"","content":"The history is documented, although the transformations are not. The selection/lead up process also isn't detailed to my knowledge. Why these eight people in particular? It wouldn't be a &quot;theme&quot; by the way, it would be an event.<br /> <br /> There are a few other possibilities of course. I've suspect full AI might exist, in a hidden form, in the Aeon setting. I think that's been hinted at in a few places after reading up on the computer sections. If such a thing exists this might be the time for it as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T02:44:09-07:00","id":677437,"title":"","content":"AI is again; something i've used in Trinity - i always assumed Novas cracked that mystery and left poorly understood artifacts - like Psuedo Gravity and Hyper-Fusion - ghosts in the machine lend some weight to the comms crunch i found. Unless i'm mistaken, Trinity suggests AI is 'impractical' not 'impossible'. I actually wrote a bit about AI's niche in 2120s technology - not that it matters.<br /> The Proxies seem to belong in Psionic Trinity, but there might be some room for early Doyen activity in a psychological setting, sure (..and back to the doyen). The only thing really missing from the Proxies story is the Doyen perspective - the stories told make it pretty clear that the benefactors remained deafeningly silent for at least a while afterwards as i remember. Although, re-reading Bue Li might shed some additional light there...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Doyen-Godwin in effect 09-25-2015, 05:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T07:11:14-07:00","id":677581,"title":"","content":"Unless we're rewriting things (which is possible, Continuum not Universe etc, etc), the Proxies are definitely 'Psionic Trinity', as Nihilist puts it. Also, not all those who could become Proxy did so. I was hinted at (can't remember where) that there were other candidates that for whatever reason didn't respond to the call or didn't make it to the meeting with the Doyen benefactors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T10:22:57-07:00","id":677752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=677581#post677581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> I was hinted at (can't remember where) that there were other candidates that for whatever reason didn't respond to the call or didn't make it to the meeting with the Doyen benefactors.</div> </div> </div> </div>What a wonderful detail... Thanks for pointing it out - nothing i remember reading ever excluded that possibility, yet i've never grasped it well enough to use it... until now.<br /> -rubs hands together-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T07:34:52-07:00","id":680001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=677752#post677752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What a wonderful detail... Thanks for pointing it out - nothing i remember reading ever excluded that possibility, yet i've never grasped it well enough to use it... until now.<br /> -rubs hands together-</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No problem. I always figured that humanity got Zweidler because the better candidate didn't answer the call. He's not just a terrible Proxy, he wasn't even the first choice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T08:28:36-07:00","id":680054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=680001#post680001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No problem. I always figured that humanity got Zweidler because the better candidate didn't answer the call. He's not just a terrible Proxy, he wasn't even the first choice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I will never not giggle at your disparagement of Zwiedler.<br /> <br /> I was trying to figure out the mysterious doyen influences over his curious leadership - but your way works and deftly avoids occams razor in the process. Elegant and funny, bravo.<br /> -smile-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T14:59:24-07:00","id":681426,"title":"","content":"Doyen just promised there would be strudel, and boom, Zweidler shows up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T05:29:46-07:00","id":681951,"title":"","content":"... violating everyone with over-familiar european greetings and failing to leave until long after the festivities - blissfully unaware of his responsibilities elsewhere.<br /> It just all lines up like a desert highway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T14:44:33-07:00","id":682362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=681951#post681951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... violating everyone with over-familiar european greetings and failing to leave until long after the festivities - blissfully unaware of his responsibilities elsewhere.<br /> It just all lines up like a desert highway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Dear lord, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T09:25:48-07:00","id":723341,"title":"","content":"Personally I like the idea of adding in what I'll just quickly call &quot;micro-continuities&quot; into the overall ball of timey-whimey stuff of this setting. I wanted to explore that stuff original with an aberrant game but sadly that fell apart due to IRL player issues. What I've been hearing about this &quot;anima&quot; on this thread seems novel and great material to build stuff on. Especially for folks who hasn't seen pretty much everything in SF before. It can also go a long way to explaining what happened to the Transhumanists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Man's unfailing capacity to believe what he prefers to be true rather than what the evidence shows to be likely and possible has always astounded me. We long for a caring Universe which will save us from our childish mistakes, and in the face of mountains of evidence to the contrary we will pin all our hopes on the slimmest of doubts. God has not been proven not to exist, therefore he must exist.</i> <b>--Academician Prokhor Zakharov</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3246-galaxy-master-zhad","name":"Galaxy Master Zhad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T13:08:49-07:00","id":724043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima#post615016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I teased one of our planned secondary settings at the Trinity Continuum/Scion/Scarred Lands panel at Gen Con. Understand that nothing's set in stone and things can still change.<br /> <br /> It's called <b>Anima</b>, and it's set in 2084 (the same year as <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Total_Recall_(1990_film)\" target=\"_blank\">Total Recall</a></i> and <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Remember_Me_(video_game)\" target=\"_blank\">Remember Me</a></i>). Other inspirations include the modern Abstergo bits of <i>Assassin's Creed</i>, and (to some degree) <i>The Matrix</i>.<br /> <br /> It's after the end of the Aberrant War, and humanity's still on the road to recovery, about 15 years before the first psions. People seek solace from the horrors of the war by using memory tech, but nothing is as straightforward as it seems on the surface.<br /> <br /> There's a reason people in <b>Aeon</b> are leery of invasive hardtech.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just going off this synopsis, I have two concerns. The first is just the name - &quot;anima&quot; is already being used in the series, as a manifestation of Taint. Its an involuntary, idiosyncratic (pseudo) hologram that some novas manifest when using their powers. Are you sure you want to re-use the term in a radically different way?<br /> <br /> The second . . . the technology for such implants almost certainly existed <i>before</i> the Aberrant War. <i>Aberrant</i> fluff mentions that direct neural interfaces (<i>a la</i> cyberjacks) were already in development (and banned by Utopia) in the early days of the Aberrant era. So it makes sense that the tech existed . . . once. However, the books also mention that Aeon and the Directive destroyed all nova research and innovations as &quot;tainted&quot; during the Aberrant War, plunging humanity into a dark age. Prototypes melted down, research notes burned, genetically engineered organisms exterminated . . . So where will the tech for the implants come from?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T13:21:37-07:00","id":724061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=724043#post724043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just going off this synopsis, I have two concerns. The first is just the name - &quot;anima&quot; is already being used in the series, as a manifestation of Taint. Its an involuntary, idiosyncratic (pseudo) hologram that some novas manifest when using their powers. Are you sure you want to re-use the term in a radically different way?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anima is being used in the original edition in this fashion, yes. The terminology we choose to use in the new edition is still in flux.<br /> <br /> Also, it's not as radically different as you might think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The second . . . the technology for such implants almost certainly existed <i>before</i> the Aberrant War. <i>Aberrant</i> fluff mentions that direct neural interfaces (<i>a la</i> cyberjacks) were already in development (and banned by Utopia) in the early days of the Aberrant era. So it makes sense that the tech existed . . . once. However, the books also mention that Aeon and the Directive destroyed all nova research and innovations as &quot;tainted&quot; during the Aberrant War, plunging humanity into a dark age. Prototypes melted down, research notes burned, genetically engineered organisms exterminated . . . So where will the tech for the implants come from? </div> </div> </div>The Trinity Universe and Trinity Continuum are not identical settings. Do not assume that minor notes and references which existed in the original books will necessarily persist in the new material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T04:58:52-07:00","id":725576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=724061#post724061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anima is being used in the original edition in this fashion, yes. The terminology we choose to use in the new edition is still in flux.<br /> <br /> Also, it's not as radically different as you might think.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's how they got me too, the word actually works for all of this and tying it all together under some kind of neotic/psychological identity/soul could be useful mataphysically to the overall cosmos. I have to admit, over-use of this particular word seemed a little strange to me as well - but i've since been mollified. I'm actually very interested in the concept and hope to see the idea make it into some material, if not the setting of 'Anima' itself. Because, this is still quite a way down the line from what i've gathered.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Trinity Universe and Trinity Continuum are not identical settings. Do not assume that minor notes and references which existed in the original books will necessarily persist in the new material. </div> </div> </div>This is making it hard for me to think about the setting in the depth i did previously. I used to have a grip on it - all two hundred years - but now? Introducing time-functions into an RPG requires a different approach to history - i can sympathise with that - i've known for a long time that the TU (as it was) would need a complete rebuild to support extended hijinx in time. But, as i think about it, i wonder to approach the whole. Mercer's Aeon was a contiguous (if bizarrely characterized in either aberrant or aeon/adventure, depending on your viewpoint) historical maypole from which players and STs could confidently draw from. Switching between groups, there might be causal disruptions and a number of less traceable changes - but within the same group the continuity was always presented as a linear line from past to present to future - but now there may not even be that.<br /> As a ST first, i'm kind of concerned as to how this is going to work - especially for Aeon/Trinity, which is at the end of two eras worth of fishtailing history, possibly more with OPP's approach. Don't get me wrong, i'm still looking forward to it - but this realization has left me a little hesitant to venture any predictions. History is now fluid - the 'Aeon' part of the setting has been redefined - continuity may not apply in some cases, it's a bit of a headache to think about frankly and i cannot wait to hear some more details on how it will all function together.<br /> Time travel is baroque, complicated and unintuitive with too many possibilities to neatly organize into possibilities - which is what makes it such a compelling story element. On the most fundamental level, it's playing with fire in a causal storytelling approach.<br /> -pyromaniacal grin-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T05:51:43-07:00","id":725675,"title":"","content":"At the risk of running very, very much away of the sure track into who-knows-what, but would cyberpunk-influenced anime like AD Police, Cyber City Oedo 808, Bubblegum Crisis or Armitage fit into either Aeon or Anima? I'm kind of curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T06:34:20-07:00","id":725777,"title":"","content":"The ties of Aeon/Trinity into 90s anime remain viable to this day, I also found the FSA in particular a very easy setting to insert stray cyberpunk influence into - other places, not always so much. After the Matrix was brought up as an influence - i have a hard time ignoring the possibility of the same niches at least to be found in what little we know of Anima, so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T17:17:11-07:00","id":727441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=725675#post725675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the risk of running very, very much away of the sure track into who-knows-what, but would cyberpunk-influenced anime like AD Police, Cyber City Oedo 808, Bubblegum Crisis or Armitage fit into either Aeon or Anima? I'm kind of curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is really too early to tell, but as a baseline, no. Most of these stories with some exceptions function the role of robots and cyborgs in a major way, and intelligent robots as well as robots in general were largely absent from the original Trinity. There overall role in Anima is currently up-for-grabs, so that is anyone's guess. Personally I don't think so, but we might be surprised.<br /> <br /> The exception would likely be Cyber-City Odeo 808, which would be pretty trivial to do in Aeon. The rest are all essentially sci-fi action crime dramas, and if you want an action crime-drama, that can be done in all of the currently announced settings with a slightly different flavor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T07:54:53-07:00","id":728888,"title":"","content":"Smart self-aware robots might be a bit much (though one can always tinker with some &quot;ghost in the machine&quot; scenarios of AIs controlling dumbbots to wave some it away), but what about power armors, mechs and cybernetics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T08:29:42-07:00","id":729022,"title":"","content":"I love a good Cyber-punk style setting. As far as RPG's go there are only a handful. In a sense I can see this setting being the stage were Humanity having witness the power of the Novas, knowing they are still out there, they are trying to obtain the powers of the Gods they chased off. The only means at their disposal is artificial, mechanical, and self modification. The biggest issue going forward is not going far enough with it. Cyber-Punk requires a total commitment to the idea of transhumanism. Humanity evolved by and through technology. The means tons of cyber-ware, bio-ware, tech items, matrix style internet manipulation are a must. I think that having a bit more history that fills in the gaps between Aberrant and Aeon will be interesting. We may even get to see some of the first stages of Project Pandora. Or those stages are a reaction to this setting. Either way it sounds interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8742-malikjack","name":"Malikjack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T15:18:10-07:00","id":733199,"title":"","content":"Power armor/mechs was a minor part of the setting-I believe the VARGs are somewhere between the two-but one that didn't get featured all that much except very early on. Cybernetics were mostly not a thing, really. I believe cybernetics are mentioned in passing in regards to Japan/Nippon, but this wasn't ever expanded upon in detail that I recall.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cyber-Punk requires a total commitment to the idea of transhumanism. </div> </div> </div>Really, cyberpunk is the <i>opposite</i> of transhumanism. The tenants of cyberpunk is that increasing technology leads to a loss of humanity and a disconnect of the natural world. Life becomes cheap and disposable. Machines and technology dominate, and people must become machines in order to survive and compete economically. Rebellion and revolution is necessary to prevent all of humanity from essentially squandering itself. We will be little better than robots, and it'll suck.<br /> <br /> Transhumanism, on the flip side, states that technology is wonderful and freeing, and that we wouldn't become inhuman, but better than human - free from fear, free from prejudice, immortal and possibly truly free. We'll all be robots, and it'll be awesome.<br /> <br /> So, the thing about Anima is whether the game chooses to illustrate the technology in revolves around as something ultimately glorious and freeing, or something destructive and dangerously distracting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T17:30:07-07:00","id":733465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=733199#post733199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Power armor/mechs was a minor part of the setting-I believe the VARGs are somewhere between the two-but one that didn't get featured all that much except very early on. Cybernetics were mostly not a thing, really. I believe cybernetics are mentioned in passing in regards to Japan/Nippon, but this wasn't ever expanded upon in detail that I recall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent analysis, Wolfgar. Cyberpunk is indeed more about the departing from humanity than the becoming a transhuman entity.<br /> Just a minor correction, the cyberware in Asia Ascendant is about half as extensive as the whole super-science chapter in Adventure! (5pages for cyberware vs 10 for super-science) - while i think i follow your drive that it was semi-unofficial and never really much mentioned before - the cyberware rules form a solid base from which to infer more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T19:40:34-07:00","id":733720,"title":"","content":"...so yes, five pages in a book that was never published.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T05:04:56-08:00","id":748932,"title":"","content":"I found the old Trinity Universe to actually be a very Safe Tech setting, probably in part due to the Aeon Society's meddling. It struck me as a natural cultural reaction to the Aberrant War that humanity and all its foibles would become the social high standard. Afterall many folk who had lived through the Nova era would look back on the superhumans with disgust and pity rather then envy. So the human ideal would shift towards embracing humanity as is rather then going after some warped ideal of perfection.<br /> Of course you would get outliers, cultures do differ after all, like the Japanese who turned into something frankly startling compared to the rest of the world. Anima seems to play with the idea of an emerging counter culture being born in the after years of the Aberrant War, when people are suffering all across the world and life doesn't seem to really be getting better, escaping into VR or painting the harshness of reality over with AR seems natural then take that further with people who just want to forget the terrible things in the world and your stage is set for stories that would have made Philip K. Dick proud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Man's unfailing capacity to believe what he prefers to be true rather than what the evidence shows to be likely and possible has always astounded me. We long for a caring Universe which will save us from our childish mistakes, and in the face of mountains of evidence to the contrary we will pin all our hopes on the slimmest of doubts. God has not been proven not to exist, therefore he must exist.</i> <b>--Academician Prokhor Zakharov</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3246-galaxy-master-zhad","name":"Galaxy Master Zhad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T09:06:53-08:00","id":1190685,"title":"","content":"So basically this would be a Talents-dominated era with mind-manipulating hardtech run rampant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-01-2018, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T00:10:33-08:00","id":1190914,"title":"","content":"Does Anima have anything to with the Possession Crisis mentioned in the Aberrant Cult write up? I know it happened earlier in the timeline (before the Shanghai Accords) but...<br /> Also is &quot;Doll house&quot; inspiration for the Anima era?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 03-08-2018, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T20:09:21-07:00","id":1197855,"title":"","content":"Now that we've seen the official timeline (at least &quot;official&quot; as in &quot;the events that precede that Aeon setting&quot;; not &quot;official&quot; as in &quot;the inescapable events that follow Aberrant or any other earlier setting&quot;), and it's referenced how this tech gets outlawed, I do wonder...<br /> <br /> 1) Is it illegal in Nippon, or does it fall in the genre of cybertech in-play there that the rest of the world doesn't use?<br /> <br /> 2) Are illegal memory tech blackmarkets a thing in the Aeon era?<br /> <br /> 3) If this tech's dominance in the Anima era hadn't been cracked down on - what would the odds have been of the world heading into a Dollhouse style Neuropocalypse?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T06:22:52-07:00","id":1197954,"title":"","content":"1) I'd say that it's either illegal or heavily regulated in Nippon.<br /> 2) The thing about letting a genie out of the bottle is that you can't or it back in. Yes, a black market for invasive mental hardtech would be a thing in \u00c6on.<br /> 3) My understanding is that this tech was cracked down on precisely because a Dollhouse-style neuropocalypse was narrowly avoided.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}